Sammy the Demigoddess (Male Chaotic Doppelganger Rogue, ascended minus
his masculine appurtenances) went to her reward with 8609752 points,
having genocided 40 species and used 13 wishes.

Highlights:

Whisperfeet found in shop around the 20th level.  I stuck with 'em on
the theory that artifacts are more resistant to cursing.

The dungeon was full of altars, including three aligned priests (one
co-aligned, in Minetown.)  The lowest was on 39, and the Castle was on
44.  This came in handy when I was preparing for the final dive.

This being my first Slash'EM game, I decided to experiment with
firearms.  My +5 assualt rifle named Demogorgonbane wound up being very
important to this character's success.

I got started when I found a sniper rifle (I thought those weren't
supposed to load?) in Grund's castle on a sergeant and went around
shooting yellow molds &c in order to get my skill up to Expert.  One of
the officers in the Castle had an assault rifle.  I eventually stacked
up and identified 580 bullets, which, enchanted to +5, sent One-Eyed
Sam and all of the demon lords to their next lives.  It proved a good
weapon against Rodney, too.  It accuracy was far superior to that of a
wand of death, and one to two bursts was always enough to put him away.
 I still had about 150 +5 bullets left at ascension, and my +7 Bat from
Hell was actually stowed in the Wallet of Perseus.

Lots of throne wishes and genocides this game.  I didn't wish for any
artifacts, and I don't think I would have gotten any, considering the
huge numbers of artifacts in Slash'EM.  3 "oLS in bag, by the end of
the game.

I ditched my extra wands in a pond in Gehennom to make room for ammo
and gems.  I wound up with 104 rubies, 26 diamonds, 15 sapphires, 7
dilithium crystals, and another four dozen or so assorted gems.  I
ascended with Thiefbane in my bag - by the time I had a deep dragon
scale mail to avoid the draining effect, I was no longer interested in
melee weapons.  I had thought that perhaps its instakill-vs-@ effect
would come in valuable against Rodney.  Maybe with a more
melee-oriented character.

After playing this game, I think that doppelgangers make dicey rogues,
because:

a) Rogues cannot get a carried magic-resistance item without artifact
wishing, which means that past the middlegame, you can only safely
polyself into undeads (or possibly xorns if you're careful with
telepathy.)  All it takes is one lich or titan getting lucky, and you
die of the touch of death.

b) One of a rogue's main assets is #2weapon, which doppelgangers cannot
use.

On the other hand, guaranteed poly control makes the rogues' quest
easy.  I spent a lot of time running around as a xorn in midgame,
looting the vaults to play the protection racket.  I eventually wound
up with ac -57, definitely a personal record.  I wound up with around
68000 surplus gold after looting the dungeon.  I gave it to the
minetown priest out of whimsy.

Think that's it, folks.  Any suggestions for the next game?


